<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 7.0 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 7.0 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 7.0 percent in the week to June 11 over the equivalent week a year ago, the Bank of England said. Last week the rise was 6.5 percent. (figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			     Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  21.64	  21.56	     20.213</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	 2.41	   2.49		2.016</p>
</text>
